{%- comment -%}
  fye-popups — every popup on the site, as blocks. Lives in footer-group.json,
  so one copy is available on every page.

  REPLACES `fye-guide-popups-group.json`, which was TWELVE sections, each
  wrapping a Klaviyo embed on Forms defaults (#202020 text, #1878B9 links).
  Build-state job 7.

  KLAVIYO IS GONE (Ed, 01/09/2026). The form here is Shopify's own
  `{% form 'contact' %}`, so a submission arrives as a normal store enquiry
  and no app is involved. Consequences worth knowing:

  1. NOTHING EMAILS THE GUIDE ANY MORE. Klaviyo used to. So the popup hands
     the file over itself, on the success panel, from `file_url`. A guide with
     no `file_url` says we will email it instead — true, because the
     submission reaches hello@ either way, but it is a manual send.
  2. Marketing consent is recorded IN THE MESSAGE, not as a list
     subscription — there is no list to subscribe to now.

  EVERYTHING IDENTIFYING GOES IN `contact[body]`. READ THIS BEFORE CHANGING
  ANY FIELD NAME.
  Custom `contact[Some name]` fields did NOT show usefully in the notification
  email — tested by Ed on 01/09/2026, who could not tell which of seven
  popups a submission had come from. The message BODY is always shown, so the
  body is where the answer belongs:

    - Liquid writes a fallback body naming the popup, so an enquiry is
      identifiable even with JavaScript off.
    - On submit, fye-ui.js REWRITES that body to fold in the popup name, the
      typed message, the journey answer and the consent answer as plain lines.

  The individual named fields are still submitted as well. That is belt and
  braces, not the mechanism — do not delete the body composition and rely on
  them again.

  HOW A POPUP IS OPENED
  Any element with `data-fye-popup="<key>"` opens the block whose `key`
  matches. `guide-download-block` and `fye-two-ways` already emit that
  attribute, so no template needed editing.

  The keys are the OLD KLAVIYO FORM IDS (V9eDYg, XMzNMS, …) because that is
  what those triggers still emit — `guide-download-block`'s setting is still
  called `klaviyo_form_id`. Renaming a setting ID is not safe, so the ID stays
  and its LABEL now says "Popup key". Change a key here and you must change it
  on the trigger in the same pass, or the button silently opens nothing.

  WHY <dialog> AND NOT THE THEME'S DRAWER PATTERN
  The one deliberate exception to §6's `data-fye-drawer` convention. A modal
  over a form needs a focus trap, a background made inert, and Escape — all
  three are free and correct with <dialog> + showModal(), and about forty
  lines of hand-rolled JS without it. Drawers stay as they are.

  Layout is the Klaviyo popup Ed signed off: photograph left at a third, form
  right, stacking to photo-on-top under 749px. Its champagne button is NOT
  carried over — buttons in this system are teal filled, sage on hover.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- for block in section.blocks -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign b = block.settings
    assign key = b.key | default: block.id
    assign heading = b.heading | default: 'Get in touch'
    assign btn_label = b.button_label | default: 'Send'
    assign uid = key | handleize

    comment
      The line that identifies this popup in the enquiry email. A setting, so
      the email can read differently from the on-screen heading — "Guide
      request: The Eternity Ring Guide" rather than just the title.
    endcomment
    assign email_line = b.email_subject | default: heading

    comment
      return_to brings the visitor back to the page they were on with the
      popup's key in the query string, which is how fye-ui.js knows to reopen
      THIS popup on its success panel rather than dumping them on /contact.
    endcomment
    assign ret = request.path | append: '?fyep=' | append: key
    assign journey_list = b.journey_options | split: ','
  -%}

  <dialog class="pop" id="fye-popup-{{ uid }}"
          data-fye-popup-panel="{{ key }}"
          data-fye-popup-label="{{ email_line | escape }}"
          aria-label="{{ heading | escape }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <div class="pop__in{% if b.image == blank %} pop__in--noimage{% endif %}">

      {%- if b.image != blank -%}
        <div class="pop__media">
          {{ b.image | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag:
             loading: 'lazy',
             widths: '380, 560, 760, 900',
             sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 100vw, 260px',
             alt: b.image_alt }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="pop__body">
        <button class="pop__close" type="button" data-fye-popup-close aria-label="Close">
          {%- render 'icon', name: 'close', size: 18 -%}
        </button>

        {%- form 'contact', return_to: ret, class: 'pop__form' -%}

          {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Rendered on every popup after any successful contact submission —
              the flash is not per-form. Harmless: only the popup named in the
              query string is opened, and the others stay closed.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="pop__done" data-fye-popup-done>
              <p class="eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow | default: 'For Your Eternity' }}</p>
              <h2 class="pop__title">{{ b.success_heading | default: 'Thank you' }}</h2>
              <div class="pop__intro">{{ b.success_body | default: '<p>We have your details.</p>' }}</div>

              {%- if b.file_url != blank -%}
                <a class="btn btn--block" href="{{ b.file_url }}">
                  {%- render 'icon', name: 'download', size: 18 -%}
                  {{ b.download_label | default: 'Download the guide' }}
                </a>
              {%- elsif b.no_file_note != blank -%}
                <p class="pop__note">{{ b.no_file_note }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

          {%- else -%}

            {%- if b.eyebrow != blank -%}
              <p class="eyebrow">{{ b.eyebrow }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            <h2 class="pop__title">{{ heading }}</h2>
            {%- if b.intro != blank -%}
              <div class="pop__intro">{{ b.intro }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if form.errors -%}
              <div class="pop__errors" role="alert">
                <p>{{ form.errors | default_errors }}</p>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="pop__field">
              <label for="pop-first-{{ uid }}">First name</label>
              <input id="pop-first-{{ uid }}" type="text" name="contact[First name]" autocomplete="given-name" placeholder="First name">
            </div>

            <div class="pop__field">
              <label for="pop-last-{{ uid }}">Last name</label>
              <input id="pop-last-{{ uid }}" type="text" name="contact[Last name]" autocomplete="family-name" placeholder="Last name">
            </div>

            <div class="pop__pair">
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-email-{{ uid }}">Email address</label>
                <input id="pop-email-{{ uid }}" type="email" name="contact[email]" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@email.com" required>
              </div>
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-phone-{{ uid }}">Telephone <span class="pop__opt">(optional)</span></label>
                <input id="pop-phone-{{ uid }}" type="tel" name="contact[Telephone]" autocomplete="tel" placeholder="For a personal follow-up">
              </div>
            </div>

            {%- if b.show_journey and journey_list.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-journey-{{ uid }}">{{ b.journey_label | default: 'Where you are in your journey' }}</label>
                <select id="pop-journey-{{ uid }}" name="contact[Journey]" data-fye-popup-journey>
                  <option value="">Please choose…</option>
                  {%- for opt in journey_list -%}
                    {%- assign opt_clean = opt | strip -%}
                    <option value="{{ opt_clean | escape }}">{{ opt_clean }}</option>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </select>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              The message box. On an enquiry it is the whole point; on a guide
              request it is noise, so it is a per-popup switch.

              It is NOT named contact[body] — the body is composed on submit
              and would overwrite whatever was typed here. fye-ui.js folds this
              value into the body instead.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if b.show_message -%}
              <div class="pop__field">
                <label for="pop-message-{{ uid }}">{{ b.message_label | default: 'What can we help with?' }}</label>
                <textarea id="pop-message-{{ uid }}" name="contact[Message]" rows="4" data-fye-popup-message
                          placeholder="{{ b.message_placeholder | default: 'A piece you have seen, a budget, a date to work to…' | escape }}"></textarea>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if b.show_consent -%}
              <label class="pop__consent" for="pop-consent-{{ uid }}">
                <input id="pop-consent-{{ uid }}" type="checkbox" name="contact[Happy to be emailed]" value="Yes" data-fye-popup-consent>
                <span>{{ b.consent_text | default: "Yes, I'm happy for For Your Eternity to email me occasional news. I can unsubscribe anytime." }}</span>
              </label>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              THE field that makes an enquiry identifiable. Liquid writes a
              usable fallback; fye-ui.js rewrites it on submit with the typed
              message and the answers folded in. Never remove the value here —
              it is what a visitor with JavaScript off sends.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="contact[body]" value="{{ email_line | escape }}" data-fye-popup-body>

            <button class="btn btn--block pop__submit" type="submit">{{ btn_label }}</button>

            {%- if b.reassurance != blank -%}
              <p class="pop__note">{{ b.reassurance }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

          {%- endif -%}

        {%- endform -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>
{%- endfor -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* ---- the dialog itself -------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .pop {
  width: min(760px, calc(100vw - (2 * var(--pad-x))));
  max-width: none;
  max-height: calc(100vh - (2 * var(--s8)));
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--ink);
  overflow: hidden;
}
/* ::backdrop does not reliably inherit custom properties across engines, so
   the token's value is repeated as a fallback. */
.fye .pop::backdrop { background: var(--scrim, rgba(35, 61, 71, 0.42)); }
.fye dialog.pop:not([open]) { display: none; }

/* A third to the photograph, as the signed-off design. */
.fye .pop__in { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr; min-height: 0; }
.fye .pop__in--noimage { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }

.fye .pop__media { position: relative; background: var(--ivory); }
.fye .pop__media :where(img) { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }

.fye .pop__body {
  position: relative;
  padding: var(--s7);
  overflow-y: auto;
  max-height: calc(100vh - (2 * var(--s8)));
}

.fye .pop__close {
  position: absolute;
  top: var(--s3);
  right: var(--s3);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 44px;
  height: 44px;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: var(--ink);
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .pop__close:hover { color: var(--sage); }

/* ---- words -------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .pop__title { margin: var(--s2) 0 var(--s3); font-size: var(--fs-h3); }
.fye .pop__intro { margin-bottom: var(--s5); font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.fye .pop__intro :where(p:last-child) { margin-bottom: 0; }

/* ---- fields ------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* Inputs, selects, textareas and the 48px minimum come from fye-core's form
   rules; only the stacking and the pair are this section's business. */
.fye .pop__form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s4); }
.fye .pop__field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
.fye .pop__pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--s4); }
.fye .pop__opt { font-weight: var(--fw-light); letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; }
/* Shorter than the site default: a popup has to stay on screen. */
.fye .pop__field :where(textarea) { min-height: 96px; }

/* The consent line is sentence case and small — the only label in the theme
   that is not an uppercase field label, because it is a sentence the visitor
   reads, not a name for a box. */
.fye .pop__consent {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--s3);
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-light);
  letter-spacing: 0;
  line-height: 1.5;
  text-transform: none;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}
.fye .pop__consent input {
  flex: 0 0 18px;
  width: 18px;
  height: 18px;
  min-height: 0;
  margin-top: 2px;
  accent-color: var(--teal);
}

.fye .pop__submit { margin-top: var(--s2); }
.fye .pop__note { margin: 0; font-size: var(--fs-fine); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); text-align: center; }

.fye .pop__errors {
  padding: var(--s3) var(--s4);
  background: var(--mist);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}
.fye .pop__errors :where(p) { margin: 0; }

/* ---- success ------------------------------------------------------------ */
.fye .pop__done { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s3); }
.fye .pop__done .btn { margin-top: var(--s3); }

/* ---- reflow: 749, the theme's own middle breakpoint --------------------- */
@media (max-width: 749px) {
  .fye .pop__in { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .fye .pop__media { height: 180px; }
  .fye .pop__media :where(img) { position: static; height: 180px; }
  .fye .pop__body { padding: var(--s5); }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .pop__pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Popups",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "popup",
      "name": "Popup",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text", "id": "key", "label": "Popup key",
          "info": "The value the button that opens this popup emits in data-fye-popup. Historically a Klaviyo form ID. Change it here and on the trigger together."
        },
        {
          "type": "text", "id": "email_subject", "label": "How this shows in the enquiry email",
          "info": "The first line of the message we receive, so you can tell which popup it came from. Falls back to the heading."
        },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Content" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph", "info": "Leave empty and the popup is the form alone, full width." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Photograph description" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "For Your Eternity" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Get in touch" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "intro", "label": "Introduction" },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Form" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Send" },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_message", "label": "Include a message box", "default": false, "info": "On for enquiries, off for guide requests." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "message_label", "label": "Message label", "default": "What can we help with?" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "message_placeholder", "label": "Message placeholder", "default": "A piece you have seen, a budget, a date to work to…" },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_journey", "label": "Ask where they are in their journey", "default": true },
        { "type": "text", "id": "journey_label", "label": "Question label", "default": "Where you are in your journey" },
        {
          "type": "textarea", "id": "journey_options", "label": "Answers",
          "info": "Comma separated.",
          "default": "Just starting to look, Ready to choose, We have a date in mind, Looking for inspiration"
        },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_consent", "label": "Show the email consent tickbox", "default": true },
        { "type": "text", "id": "consent_text", "label": "Consent wording", "default": "Yes, I'm happy for For Your Eternity to email me occasional news. I can unsubscribe anytime." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "reassurance", "label": "Line under the button", "default": "Your details are kept private and used only to reply to you." },
        { "type": "header", "content": "After sending" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "success_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Thank you" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "success_body", "label": "Message" },
        {
          "type": "url", "id": "file_url", "label": "Guide file or download page",
          "info": "Handed over immediately on the success panel. Without it the popup says the guide will be emailed."
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "download_label", "label": "Download button label", "default": "Download the guide" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "no_file_note", "label": "Wording when there is no file", "default": "We will email it to you shortly." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Popups", "blocks": [{ "type": "popup" }] }]
}
{% endschema %}
